  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/0cc9ff3d-4a0c-4578-89ae-386c6fe6e5e0-image.png\" /></p><p>As we know, the spring force will give the necessary centripetal force for rotation.</p><p>So,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mi>l</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>&nbsp;Thus, the stretch in the spring<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>l</mi><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p>",
